      "obligation": "refuter:8:1",
      "id": "lem-kernel-generators-for-the-weak-bgg-complex",
      "location": "Proof 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The step says “since im d^B_{k+1} is a subobject of B_{k+1}”. The differential is B_{k+1} → B_k, so its image is naturally a subobject of B_k and a quotient of B_{k+1}; no embedding into its source is supplied. The desired composition-factor inclusion nevertheless follows immediately from the quotient sequence 0 → ker d^B_{k+1} → B_{k+1} → im d^B_{k+1} → 0 and the additivity stated in [F4]. Thus the conclusion is valid, but the stated justification uses the wrong source/image relationship.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
